Twentieth pass: daemon admission, shared runtime pressure, and base Zsh
====================================================================

Scope: 30 new USDT contracts, nine base components, five installed profiles.
No DTrace engine, tracing transport, installed binary or running daemon change.
All new arguments are scalar: no commands, environment, credentials, capability
or reply tokens, filenames, or message payloads are collected. Runtime object
addresses are opaque process-local correlation identities, not stable IDs.

Contracts (arguments in order)
------------------------------
service_runtime (libservice):
 retry-scheduled(object, delay_ms, next_monotonic_ms): every failed result.
 retry-recovered(object, prior_delay_ms): success after nonzero backoff only.
 health-change(object, error, cumulative_failures): healthy/unhealthy boundary;
 changing from one nonzero error to another is not a health transition.
 budget-rejected(error, requested_ms): invalid interval or nested budget.
 budget-expired(overdue_ms): each timeout check after the deadline, not one
 event per budget. No added clock calls; uses the existing monotonic sample.
 lease-limit(count, capacity, error): full set or exhausted serial space.
 Ambient and runtime providers share one .d input to the base DOF link rule.

libchannel:
 queue-limit(queued_messages, queued_bytes, queued_fds): a queue ceiling rejected
 this message. Counts are current occupancy; no attempted contents are exposed.
 pending-limit(pending, maximum): request concurrency ceiling.

capsule:
 ctl-admission-failure(stage, error, current_connections): confinement=1,
 connection ceiling=2, peer credentials query=3, allocation=4, kevent watch=5.
 Ceiling error ENOSPC is a diagnostic classification, not a returned errno.
 ctl-timeout(connection_state): timer expiry before destroying the connection.
 The existing probe header now compiles out with MK_DTRACE=no, matching its
 Makefile. The enabled branch explicitly defines WITH_DTRACE.

switchboard:
 capsule-rpc-start(request_bytes, sent_fds, maximum_reply_fds)
 capsule-rpc-done(result, transport_errno): result=-1 is transport failure;
 otherwise result is Capsule application status. errno is saved and restored.
 capsule-stale-reply(one_based_attempt): rejected reply before retry/exhaustion.
 capsule-malformed-reply(received_bytes, received_fds): wire shape rejection.
 Pair RPC start/done by process/thread with a nesting stack. An event drop or
 process exit can leave an unmatched start. Profile histograms exclude it.

bsddevice:
 worker-reject(stage, error, current_workers): quota=1 (ENOSPC classification),
 allocation=2, worker startup=3, descriptor confinement/watch installation=4.
bsdextension:
 accept-retry(error): failed accept after excluding clean quiesce, before fd
 exhaustion backoff. EINTR remains visible as a retry.
 worker-reject(stage,error): session ceiling=1 (ENOSPC classification),
 allocation=2, pthread_create=3 (uses its returned error, not errno).
bsdmemory:
 dependency-health(kind,error,cumulative_failures): source sysctl=1, notify=2;
 only the existing health-change branch, providing dependency context beyond
 the generic libservice health event.
bsdsysctl:
 session-limit(global_table_full, same_label_sessions): admission refusal.
 session-open-failure(stage,error): channel setup=1, request handler install=2.
 session-close-reason(kind,error): idle=1 (ETIMEDOUT), channel=2, handler=3.
 Preserves existing cleanup and error precedence.

zsh (base runtime package):
 fork-start(job): immediately before fork; fork-done(pid,error) in both parent
 and child. Child sees pid=0; a parent/child pair is not a single latency pair.
 job-limit(table_size): existing job-table expansion rejection in zfork.
 exec-attempt(stage), exec-failure(stage,error): each actual execve invocation
 in zexecve, including interpreter fallbacks. Stages 1..6 follow source order.
 Successful exec does not return: correlate proc:::exec-success if needed.
 pipeline-start(job,how), pipeline-done(job,status,async): final status for
 foreground, launch status for background (async=1). Recursive pipelines,
 forked children and _exit paths preclude naïve thread-local latency pairing.
 wait-start(pid,wait_builtin), wait-done(pid,result): waitforpid's ordinary and
 trapped-signal return paths. Does not claim to cover every zwaitjob wait.
 Vendor sources remain buildable without the base-specific FIVEBSD_TRACE flag.

Validation
----------
18 native builds (all logical CPUs): nine components, MK_DTRACE=yes/no.
ELF DOF inspection: all 30 declared contracts have executable sites and correct
arity; none of the new providers exists in disabled builds.
Existing libservice retry/health, lease ownership, drain deadline and budget
scope tests pass in both modes (eight cases). Upstream Zsh A01grammar,
A05execution and A06assign pass in both modes (six suites). These execute
ordinary isolated workloads; no privileged system services are started.
Five profiles compile offline both unfiltered and PID/duration filtered, and
appear in the base Makefile installation list. No live probe firing is claimed:
the running host has no /dev/dtrace. Daemon failure branches are compiled and
linked, not injected into production. Kernel and boot qualification from the
nineteenth pass remains separate.

Artifacts: /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-twentieth-validation
Scripts in this directory reproduce builds, DOF checks, codegen comparisons,
existing tests and offline profile checks. No installation or reboot performed.
